@startuml 13_Group_Key_Rotation

title 13. When Conversation Member Keys Are Rotated

actor "Admin" as Admin
participant "Admin Client" as AdminClient
participant "Crypto Layer" as AdminCrypto
participant "localStorage" as AdminStorage
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Vault KV" as Vault
participant "WebSocket" as WS
participant "Member Client" as MemberClient
participant "Member Crypto" as MemberCrypto

Admin -> AdminClient: Trigger rotation\n(explicit or implicit)
activate AdminClient

alt Implicit rotation
    AdminClient --> Admin: "Rotation required - confirm?"
    Admin -> AdminClient: Confirm
end

AdminClient -> AdminCrypto: Generate new group_key
activate AdminCrypto
note right of AdminCrypto
  new_group_key = random(32 bytes)
  CSPRNG
end note
AdminCrypto --> AdminClient: new_group_key
deactivate AdminCrypto

AdminClient -> AdminCrypto: Generate new member_key
activate AdminCrypto
note right of AdminCrypto
  new_member_key = Encrypt(
    new_group_key,
    identity_secret
  )
end note
AdminCrypto --> AdminClient: new_member_key
deactivate AdminCrypto

AdminClient -> Server: GET /conversations/{conv_id}/all-tokens
activate Server
note right of Server
  Fetch ALL token versions
  for re-encryption
end note

Server -> Vault: List all versions for conversation
activate Vault
Vault --> Server: List of version names
deactivate Vault

loop For each token version
    Server -> Vault: GET version
    activate Vault
    Vault --> Server: encrypted_token (with old group_key)
    deactivate Vault
end

Server --> AdminClient: All encrypted tokens
deactivate Server

AdminClient -> AdminStorage: Get old member_key
activate AdminStorage
AdminStorage --> AdminClient: old_member_key
deactivate AdminStorage

AdminClient -> AdminCrypto: Decrypt old member_key
activate AdminCrypto
AdminCrypto --> AdminClient: old_group_key
deactivate AdminCrypto

loop For each encrypted token

    AdminClient -> AdminCrypto: Decrypt with old_group_key
    activate AdminCrypto
    note right of AdminCrypto
      token = Decrypt(
        encrypted_token,
        old_group_key
      )
    end note
    AdminCrypto --> AdminClient: token (plaintext)
    deactivate AdminCrypto
    
    AdminClient -> AdminCrypto: Re-encrypt with new_group_key
    activate AdminCrypto
    note right of AdminCrypto
      new_encrypted_token = Encrypt(
        token,
        new_group_key
      )
    end note
    AdminCrypto --> AdminClient: new_encrypted_token
    deactivate AdminCrypto
    
end

AdminClient -> AdminClient: Derive new group_key_version\n("v2" or incremented)

AdminClient -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/rotate-group-key\n{new_member_key, group_key_version, re_encrypted_tokens[]}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Verify:\n- Requester is admin\n- Permissions valid

Server -> Vault: Batch update all token versions
activate Vault

loop For each re-encrypted token
    Vault -> Vault: PUT /conversations/{conv_id}/versions/{version}\n{new_encrypted_token}
    note right of Vault
      Overwrite with new encryption
      Old tokens encrypted with old_group_key
      New tokens encrypted with new_group_key
    end note
end

Vault --> Server: All updated
deactivate Vault

Server -> DB: UPDATE conversation\nSET group_key_version = {new_version}\nSET all member_keys = NULL\n(except admin)
activate DB
note right of DB
  Set all member_keys to NULL
  except the admin who initiated
  rotation
end note
DB --> Server: Updated
deactivate DB

Server -> WS: Notify all members\n"Cache invalidation - group key rotated"
activate WS
WS -> MemberClient: Rotation notification
deactivate WS

Server --> AdminClient: "Rotation successful"
deactivate Server

AdminClient -> AdminStorage: Clear old data
activate AdminStorage
note right of AdminStorage
  Delete:
  - Old member_key
  - Old cached tokens
end note
AdminStorage --> AdminClient: Cleared
deactivate AdminStorage

AdminClient -> AdminStorage: Store new member_key
activate AdminStorage
AdminStorage --> AdminClient: Stored
deactivate AdminStorage

AdminClient --> Admin: "Rotation complete"
deactivate AdminClient

' Other members respond to notification
activate MemberClient

MemberClient -> MemberClient: Receive rotation notification

MemberClient -> MemberClient: Invalidate cache

MemberClient -> Server: GET /conversations/{conv_id}
activate Server

Server -> DB: Get conversation
activate DB
DB --> Server: {member_key: NULL,\ngroup_key_version: "v2", ...}
deactivate DB

Server --> MemberClient: Conversation data
deactivate Server

MemberClient -> MemberClient: Detect member_key == NULL

MemberClient -> MemberClient: REQUEST GROUP KEY\nfrom online member
note right of MemberClient
  Use asymmetric encryption
  (Flow 04 - Request Group Key)
  Get new_group_key from admin
  or other member who has it
end note

MemberClient -> MemberClient: Receive new_group_key

MemberClient -> MemberCrypto: Generate new member_key
activate MemberCrypto
note right of MemberCrypto
  new_member_key = Encrypt(
    new_group_key,
    identity_secret
  )
end note
MemberCrypto --> MemberClient: new_member_key
deactivate MemberCrypto

MemberClient -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/update-member-key\n{new_member_key}
activate Server

Server -> DB: UPDATE member_key\n(only if NULL)
activate DB
DB --> Server: Updated
deactivate DB

Server --> MemberClient: "Updated successfully"
deactivate Server

MemberClient --> MemberClient: "Access restored"
deactivate MemberClient

note over Admin, MemberClient
  Rotation complete:
  ✅ New group_key generated
  ✅ All tokens re-encrypted with new group_key
  ✅ All members get new group_key
  ⚠️ Temporary lockout during transition
  ⚠️ High overhead (decrypt + re-encrypt all tokens)
  ⚠️ Admin temporarily has all tokens in plaintext
  
  Security impact:
  - Old group_key compromised → still secure
  - All historical messages now protected by new key
  - Members must be online or wait for helper
end note

@enduml
